  "text": [
    "Pier fishing remained relatively slow with a few coho salmon being caught.",
    "Anglers reported that the catch improved around mid-day to the afternoon when water temps are in the high 40 to 50 degrees Fahrenheit.",
    "Fish were caught on shrimp and minnows successfully.",
    "Perch fishing out of Grand Haven has picked up.",
    "Boats have had success both south out of Grand Haven in 50-70 feet of water, and straight out of Grand Haven in 55 feet of water using spikes, wigglers, and minnows.",
    "The Chinook salmon catch has been good, with some coho salmon and brown trout mixed in.",
    "Success was found fishing the mudline from the Grand River in 40 to 55 feet of water; fish were found 30 to 40 feet deep pulling meat rigs and spoons.",
    "Good colors have been black with white, greens, and oranges.",
    "Boats going south towards Port Sheldon also found king salmon in 65 to 75 feet of water."
  ],
